  "articleBody": "Embarking on a roofing project is a significant investment, and like any big home improvement, there are common missteps you can easily sidestep with a little foresight. One frequent mistake homeowners make is accepting a vague estimate. You really want a detailed breakdown of costs, not just a lump sum. This means clarifying if things like damaged decking or flashing are included in the price. Another common pitfall is choosing materials solely based on appearance without considering our unique Texas climate. Certain materials might look great, but if they don't stand up to the sun, wind, and hail we experience, you'll regret it later. Always think about durability and manufacturer requirements, especially for warranty validity.\n\nHomeowners sometimes overlook protecting their property during the project. It's easy to forget about safeguarding landscaping, driveways, and even access points. Before work begins, discuss how the crew will protect your property and manage debris. Lastly, don't ignore the process for unexpected repairs. If the crew uncovers hidden damage, you should have a clear agreement on how those additional costs and approvals will be handled. Being proactive on these points helps ensure a smoother project and avoids unpleasant surprises.\n\n### Common Mistakes to Avoid\n*   **Vague Estimates:** Insist on a detailed, itemized quote that clearly outlines all costs and inclusions, such as decking and flashing repairs.\n*   **Ignoring Climate:** Select materials specifically designed for the demanding Texas weather, considering sun, hail, and wind resistance.\n*   **Skipping Property Protection:** Confirm with your contractor how they will protect your landscaping, driveway, and ensure site cleanliness during the project.\n*   **Unclear Change Orders:** Establish a clear process for approving and costing any additional repairs discovered once work begins.\n*   **DIY Permitting:** Don't assume you handle permits. Clarify who is responsible for obtaining all necessary local permits before construction starts.\n\nIf you're unsure about any aspect of your roofing project planning, contact us for expert guidance.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}